{
  "title": "Popliteal Artery Entrapment Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3107/popliteal-artery-entrapment-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 1 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Popliteal artery entrapment syndrome is a condition characterized by constriction of the popliteal artery by adjacent muscles, tendons or fibrous tissue.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be suspected clinically with diminished pulses with active foot plantar flexion or passive foot dorsiflexion and confirmed with a lower extremity arteriogram.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally conservative for mild symptoms with vascular surgery indicated for patients with refractory symptoms.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male predominance (about 4:1)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "patient age typically 25-40 years old",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "typically due to underlying anatomic abnormality",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "decreased blood flow distal to the popliteal fossa leading to signs and symptoms consistent with compartment syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification and Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 3,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Modified Whelan Classification**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type I",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Medial head of the gastrocnemius is normal but the popliteal artery runs in an aberrant course",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3107/images/popliteal%20artery.jpg",
                          "caption": "Illustrations showing the different classifications of popliteal artery entrapment syndrome and the relevant anatomy"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type II",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Medial head of the gastrocnemius is located laterally, no deviation of popliteal artery",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3107/images/popliteal%20artery.jpg",
                          "caption": "Illustrations showing the different classifications of popliteal artery entrapment syndrome and the relevant anatomy"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type III",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "There is an abnormal muscle bundle from the medial head of the gastrocnemius that surrounds and constricts the popliteal artery",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3107/images/popliteal%20artery.jpg",
                          "caption": "Illustrations showing the different classifications of popliteal artery entrapment syndrome and the relevant anatomy"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type IV",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Popliteal artery is entrapped by the popliteus muscle",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3107/images/popliteal%20artery.jpg",
                          "caption": "Illustrations showing the different classifications of popliteal artery entrapment syndrome and the relevant anatomy"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type V",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Popliteal vein is entrapped with the popliteal artery in any of the above scenarios",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3107/images/popliteal%20artery.jpg",
                          "caption": "Illustrations showing the different classifications of popliteal artery entrapment syndrome and the relevant anatomy"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "swelling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "patients often report limb swelling as primary complaint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "paresthesias",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "foot numbness and paresthesias also common",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tingling sensation of toes following vigorous exercise",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cramping",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "calf cramping following even light exercise as the condition worsens",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "limbs can occasionally be asymptomatic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**diminished pulses** with active foot plantar flexion or passive foot dorsiflexion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "coolness of posterior calf and paresthesias may also be present",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can easily be confused with posterior compartment syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually normal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Doppler ultrasound",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "less invasive than arteriogram",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "useful during physical exam to detect changes in pulse when active plantar flexion or passive dorsiflexion is performed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Arteriogram",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3107/images/popliteal%20artery%20entrapment%20syndrome%20image.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "used to confirm diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "close to 100% sensitivity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**will show stenosis, obliteration and post-stenotic dilation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI/MRA and CT/CTA",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "studies ongoing to evaluate usefulness for detection of popliteal artery entrapment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "activity modification and observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "mild symptoms with rigorous exercise only",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "vascular bypass with saphenous vein vs endarterectomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if damage to the popliteal artery or vein",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "most patients eventually require surgery",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "can perform posterior or medial approach to popliteal fossa",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "posterior approach provides improved exposure",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "medial approach used more when bypass is indicated",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "structures released depend on the type of entrapment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Surgical failure**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "30% rate of return of entrapment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can result in need for amputation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Wound infection**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "<5%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**DVT**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "around 10%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "70-100% of patients are reported to be asymptomatic after surgery",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
